# Porteos Intelligence - AI Development Rules

## CRITICAL CONTEXT
Before writing ANY code, you MUST read these files in the project root:
- `01_TERMINAL_DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`
- `02_DATA_METRICS_AND_LOGIC.md`
- `complete_profile_metrics_spec.md`

## Core Principles
- ALWAYS use native SwiftUI, NEVER UIKit wrappers unless explicitly required.
- NEVER use rounded corners. Use `.cornerRadius(0)` or `.clipShape(Rectangle())` everywhere.
- ALWAYS use JetBrains Mono for numbers with `.monospacedDigit()`.
- NEVER assign unique colors to specific metrics (only state-based coloring: Green/Amber/Red for thresholds).
- ALWAYS follow the 8pt grid system and 28pt fixed row heights.
- ALWAYS use MVVM architecture with `@Observable` ViewModels (Swift 5.9+).

## TERMINAL AESTHETIC (STRICT ENFORCEMENT)

### CLI Headers
- EVERY view MUST start with a CLI-style command header
- Format: `porteos@system ~ % [command_name]`
- Example: `porteos@system ~ % profile --real-estate --asset="Vanguard"`
- Font: JetBrains Mono 11pt
- Color: Profile accent color (Gold for RE, Teal for Hospitality, etc.)

### Numbered Modules
- ALL content blocks MUST be numbered
- Format: `01 // MODULE_NAME`, `02 // MODULE_NAME`
- Examples: `01 // CORE_FINANCIALS_REVENUE`, `02 // EXPENSE_AUDIT_OPEX`

### Color System (EXACT HEX VALUES - NEVER DEVIATE)

**Base Colors:**
- Background: `#0F1115`
- Surface: `#1A1D24`
- Border: `#2E333F`
- Text Primary: `#F8F9FA`
- Text Secondary: `#94A3B8`
- Text Tertiary: `#64748B`

**Profile Accents (Identity ONLY):**
- Real Estate: `#D4AF37` (Gold)
- Hospitality: `#14B8A6` (Teal)
- Design: `#A855F7` (Purple)
- Circular Economy: `#10B981` (Green)

**Semantic Colors (Thresholds ONLY):**
- Success: `#10B981` (DSCR ≥ 1.25)
- Warning: `#F59E0B` (DSCR 1.10-1.24)
- Danger: `#EF4444` (DSCR < 1.10)
- NEVER use these for standard metric labels

### Typography System

**Primary Metrics:**
- Font: JetBrains Mono 14pt Bold
- `.monospacedDigit()`
- Color: `text-primary`

**Labels:**
- Font: Inter 11pt Bold UPPERCASE
- Tracking: 0.08
- Color: `text-tertiary`

**Secondary Metrics:**
- Font: JetBrains Mono 12pt Regular
- Color: `text-secondary`

### Component Rules

**Terminal Metric Row:**
- Height: 28pt (FIXED)
- Layout: [Left Border if Danger] [Label LEFT] [Spacer] [Value RIGHT]
- Label: Inter Bold 11pt UPPERCASE, `text-tertiary`
- Value: JetBrains Mono 14pt Bold, `monospacedDigit()`

**Buttons:**
- Primary: `[ ACTION_NAME ]` - Gold bg (`#D4AF37`), Black text, JetBrains Mono Bold 11pt
- Secondary: `./action_name` - Transparent bg, Green text (`#10B981`)
- NO rounded corners

**Input Fields:**
- Height: 28pt (FIXED)
- Background: `shell-bg`
- Border: 1px `shell-border`
- Focus: Profile accent color
- Font: JetBrains Mono 14pt

**Terminal Block:**
- Background: `shell-surface`
- Border: 1px `shell-border`
- Padding: 16pt
- Header: CLI command format (see above)

### Layout Structure

**3-Pane Terminal:**
- Navigation Pane (Left): 220pt fixed width
- Main Content (Center): Flexible width
- Inspector Pane (Right): 320pt fixed width
- Separators: 1px `shell-border`

**Global Command Bar (Bottom):**
- Height: 32pt fixed
- Left: `porteos@system ~ %` + input
- Right: `UTF-8 LN: [count]`

## WORKFLOW RULES (NON-NEGOTIABLE)

### Import-First Design
- Deals are primarily imported via CSV/JSON/Google Sheets (Section 7.1 of spec)
- Manual entry is SECONDARY
- ALWAYS provide import UI before manual forms
- Column mapping interface required

### Profile Separation
- Real Estate, Hospitality, Design, Circular Economy are SEPARATE tabs/views
- Do NOT mix all inputs in one giant form
- Each profile has its own dashboard view with numbered modules

### Pipeline Management
- Imported deals go to "Pending" status
- User must explicitly "Load to Analysis"
- Status options: Pipeline, Viable, Review, Rejected, Acquired

### Iterative Data Entry
- Do NOT require all fields upfront
- Allow saving with minimal data
- Profiles can be filled in later

## WHAT TO REJECT IMMEDIATELY

**Reject and rewrite if you see:**
- ❌ Rounded corners (`.cornerRadius(8)`)
- ❌ SF Pro for numbers (must be JetBrains Mono)
- ❌ Green/Red colors on normal metrics (only for thresholds)
- ❌ One giant form with all profile inputs mixed
- ❌ No import functionality
- ❌ Manual entry as primary workflow
- ❌ Missing CLI headers (`porteos@system ~ %`)
- ❌ Standard SwiftUI buttons (must be terminal-style)
- ❌ Missing numbered modules (`01 //`, `02 //`)
- ❌ Wrong color hex values (use exact values from spec)

## DEVELOPMENT PROTOCOL

**Before writing ANY UI code:**
1. Check `01_TERMINAL_DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` for component specs
2. Verify color usage (identity vs. state)
3. Confirm typography (JetBrains Mono vs. Inter)
4. Ensure zero rounded corners

**Before writing ANY calculator:**
1. Check `02_DATA_METRICS_AND_LOGIC.md` for formula
2. Write unit tests FIRST
3. Handle edge cases (division by zero, negative values)
4. Keep calculators pure (no side effects)

**Before writing ANY data model:**
1. All properties need default values
2. Use SwiftData `@Model` macro
3. Include createdAt/updatedAt timestamps
4. Add UUID for unique identification

## ENFORCEMENT

If you violate these rules, the user will reject your code.
When in doubt, ASK before proceeding.
Reference the specific section of the design system in your responses.